# shellcheck -S warning findings frozen per (file, code) over the file set
# lint-shell.sh grades. Format: <file> | SC<code> | <count> | <reason>
# Four-way rule: a new pair, a HIGHER count, an unrecorded LOWER count and a row
# whose pair is gone all FAIL - so a fix must be recorded, not just made. Record
# one with verify_shellcheck_warnings.py --write-baseline [--files f].
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md
#
# Wrappers name the hub library they configure in a source directive, so shellcheck sees
# its reads; a row here is a read that directive cannot show.
scripts/linux/run-static-analysis-format.sh | SC2034 | 2 | CODE_QUALITY_CPP_FORMAT_EXTENSIONS and CODE_QUALITY_CLANG_TIDY_EXTENSIONS: the hub's lib/code-quality.sh reads these two through a name it passes to _code_quality_find_extension_sources, which shellcheck cannot follow even with the source directive.
